    "file": "Categories/04. Event/04.02 Modern Crisis and Timeline/04.02.07 The Era of the Great Disappearance.MD",
    "title": "The Era of the Great Disappearance",
    "text": "The Era of the Great Disappearance defines the contemporary crisis caused by the recent physical thickening of the pale encircling the Insulindian Isola. Long range radiocomputer operators and interisolary telegraph stations in Revachol have received high latency transmissions from distant observatories, confirming that foreign governments across Mundi, Graad, and Seol are facing the exact same catastrophic phenomenon. Across Elysium, the perimeter of entropic un-matter has expanded and grown dramatically denser, rendering trans-isolary crossing exceptionally hazardous and prompting international state emergencies.\n\nIn response, Coalition authorities and foreign states have placed trans-isolary border crossings under strict military lockdown. Non-specialized civilian transit across the pale is completely inaccessible, banned outside of dire state emergencies. Crossing outer pale corridors requires rare government military permits, specialized compressional aerostats, and heavily shielded transport vehicles. Trans-isolary trade continues only at a sluggish, restricted pace. Crews returning from cross-pale routes must endure mandatory quarantine and medical screening for pale exposure, while vehicles undergo extensive refitting and decontamination.\n\nWithin the geographic borders of the Insulindian Isola itself, domestic travel remains completely fine. Citizens, dockworkers, and merchants can move freely inland, navigate coastal waterways, and traverse the districts of Revachol without bureaucratic hindrance. However, genuine fear of the thickened pale has reshaped everyday culture. Ordinary residents avoid discussing or dwelling upon other isolas simply out of pragmatic dread, reluctant to contemplate the terrifying void tightening around their world. Outside of radiocomputer experts and logistics professionals, public conversation regarding distant lands has ceased, cementing an intense regional focus across Martinaise and Jamrock.",
